Jesse Holland wrote:
> Here's my question:
>
> Up until now, I've relied on Finger of Death and Magic Missile to kill
> everyone (if they resist FoD, Magic Missile always works).
>
> Will there be some nasties in the last four levels - nasties like Death
> - for which those spells won't work?

You are correct, Finger of Death won't work on Death.  In fact it will
have the opposite result you desire.  But Magic Missile will work fine.


I don't want to give too much away, but my main strategy is to avoid
the Riders as much as possible.  Especially Pestilence.  There are some
ways to lure them to areas you want them and to block them in, but I
won't give away any more than that.

> Because I have no long range weapon aside from those spells.  Close
> range is MagicBane.

Sounds like a good strategy so far.

> Also, feel free to comment on the following weaknesses of this possible
> ascension:
> -notable exceptions from this game include no wand of cancellation, no
> spellbook of remove curse

Lots of blessed scrolls of remove curse are better than the spell,
since you'll want to avoid spending magic power unless you need it.
Also the scroll will take care of other cursed items you're not
directly wearing, like your luckstone, unicorn horn and bag of holding.


> -my helmet is only an ordinary helmet+3

You seem to be doing fine with it on, but it penalizes your
spellcasting.  If you're not significantly disadvantaged in
spellcasting by the helmet you may as well leave it on I suppose.
There is definitely better headwear for a wizard in the game.

> -my HP is 231, will try to raise it with alchemy

Good idea.  You might want to stash a couple blessed potions of gain
energy, since you'll be using Magic Missle a lot.  You could find
yourself out of power at inopportune times.

> -no pet

They don't tend to last long in the endgame anyway, and in fact they
usually slow you down.

Good luck!



